WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.133
-It is great to see you, buddy,

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.167
and thank you
for playing Password.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.634
-So much fun.
-I appreciate that.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:05.934
It's been a while since you --
since you've been on the show.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.067
-I know, yeah.
It's been a long time.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.701
-Yeah, we always
have a good time.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.734
-Yeah. But, you know,
I've been watching the show.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.133
I love the show, and --
-Appreciate that.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.934
-So tonight -- I haven't
been here in a long time,

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.868
and I just wanted
to show you my appreciation.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.133
So I brought a gift.
-You don't have to do that.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.968
-No, but I thought it's kind of
like a gesture, so --

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.667
Because I watch the show
and I love everything you do.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.634
I love all the taped segments
and the live segments,

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.767
like what you did tonight,

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.067
so I thought I would
just present the show --

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.767
This is for the show.
It's not for you personally.

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.234
-Okay.
-It's for the production,

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:36.601
but it's a check for, you know,
$1,400 and a little more --

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.734
$1,433.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:39.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.300
-Wow. This is --

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.567
-And I need to explain, maybe,
just the amount.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:48.834
-This is $1,433
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.868
-To "The Jimmy Fallon Show,"
actually.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:53.667
-Oh, yeah, well, you can --
we can change that, but, uh...

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.667
-That's very sweet of you.
This is --

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.801
-I just -- I thought --
-Why that amount?

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.701
-I was talking to
my business accountant.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:02.100
He said this is kind of
what I can afford right now.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.367
But the other --
-A scrape.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:05.767
-Well, and I thought when
you're expecting nothing,

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.000
It's kinda like --
-Wow.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.834
-I mean, obviously
it's all relative, you know.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:09.934
-No, this is a --

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.100
-Some people might
donate more, but --

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.434
-$1,433. No.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:13.901
-The thing is, you're going to
get hammered on taxes

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.901
when you take this, so, like,
it's gonna end up being

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:18.200
kind of like $750 that you net.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.067
And that's why I aimed it
for this -- for this figure.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:22.901
-This is unbelievable.
This is so thoughtful.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.868
I think you might be
the first person ever...

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:25.901
-Well, that's what I thought.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.434
-...donate money
to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:28.534
-It's a nice thing to do.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.234
You can use it
for production costs,

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.467
which is what's written here,
"For production."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.901
-Yes, "For production."
This is so sweet of you.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.734
-Rent some nice costumes
or something

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.133
and do, like, a funny sketch.
I don't know.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.267
-I don't know
what to do with this.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:38.601
But we're going to
do something with it.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.000
-You can frame it if you want,
put it in your office.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.634
But the thing is, this is worth
so much more than $1,433,

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.100
because if you have, like,
someone like Mark Cuban

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.334
on the show,
which I'm sure you've had...

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.701
-Yeah.
-...you know, Mark Cuban

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.334
has like $2 billion, I believe.
-Yeah, that's correct.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:50.901
-And so, you know --
-He's watching.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:53.701
-A million dollars is like
a thousand dollars, you know,

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:54.868
for you and me to Mark --

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.367
I mean, how much money
do you have?

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.968
I mean, but for me, like,
you know, like, he has so much,

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.767
and he'll see this and he'll
see, like, the, you know --

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.968
You'll put this on YouTube, and,
like, he'll see the comments.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.868
Everyone will be like, "Wow,
Michael's this fantastic guy."

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.167
-Yeah.
-And he'll be like...

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.501
-"I want to be a fantastic guy."
-..."I want to do it,"

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:10.634
and he'll bring you --
-Mark Cuban.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.033
-Who knows what kind of check
he'll cut?

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
-This is smart.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.133
That is so smart.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:19.734
-Well, the last thing
to say about it

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.033
is that it's not, like,
actually a check.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.267
It's a deposit slip.
But that's only because --

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.701
I talked to a guy, and he said,
"Don't put --

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.200
They'll will see your
account number on TV.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.400
Don't do that."
So this is largely symbolic.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.667
And, like, I'll Venmo --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.267
You know,
we'll figure it out later.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.133
Whatever.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.400
We'll figure it out later.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.501
-This is a symbolic gift.

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.234
-Well, that's what --
When they do the big checks,

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:41.834
it's not a real check.
It's a symbol.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:44.868
-So it's similar
to a giant cardboard check.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:45.868
It's this.
I appreciate it.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.033
-And that's how I show love.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.734
So, if it's not good enough,
then whatever.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.167
-No!
No, of course.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.601
Oh, my gosh, nothing but love.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.734
Michael Cera.
[ Applause ]

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:54.934
Thank you very much.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.234
Thank you very much.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:03:00.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.033
-You want me to hold it, too?

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.501
-Yeah, you hold it there.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:11.934
-Hey, I-I know -- I just want
to say congratulations.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:14.067
Since I've seen you,
you've become a dad.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.334
-Yes.
-How's fatherhood?

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:16.968
Congratulations, buddy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.334
You're an amazing dad.
Are you loving it?

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:21.901
How old's baby?
-He's 11 months old.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.534
-Wow.
-He's almost one.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.300
-Yeah, saying words?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.968
-No, he kind of, like,
grasps at making sounds.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.467
Like, he has said "dada,"

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.100
but I kind of don't have, like,
enough points on the graph yet

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.434
to know if he actually knows
what he's saying when he says it

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.367
or if he's just making sounds.
-Doesn't matter. It counts.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.400
-But it feels good.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:41.667
-If it sounds like "Dada,"
just have it be Dada, yeah.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.167
-Yeah, and I just -- I love him.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.434
And I know he'll
be watching this someday

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.834
and just be so proud of me,

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.467
how well I did tonight
and everything.

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.567
-He will.
He will see the love.

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.067
It's just --
That's symbolic, you know.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.267
-I love him.
-How much love --

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.534
-I love you, son.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.934
-Now, I want to
talk about this movie,

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.701
'cause this is for children.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:03.000
-This is "Paws of Fury:
The Legend of Hank."

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.634
-Yes.
-I love the name.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:06.767
I love "Paws of Fury:
The Legend of Hank."

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.834
But then I also was doing
a little research on this.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.734
It's produced by Mel Brooks.
-Mel Brooks.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:13.501
-Who's one of my comedy heroes.
-Me too.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.901
-And he does a voice, as well?

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:16.901
-He's so funny in it.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.334
-Did you meet Mel Brooks?

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.200
-You know, I never met him
in relation to this project,

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.067
but I actually met him, like,
years ago

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:23.434
just randomly when I was --

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:25.234
I was working
on the Culver City lot.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.133
And he has an office there,
and I was with my friend.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.734
He said, "Why don't we
just go say hi to Mel?"

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.100
And so we went over,
and he had us in his office

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.167
for like an hour.
-He was just there?

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.000
-Yeah, and he was happy
to have us.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.033
The first thing he said to me,
he went,

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.934
"Hey, thanks for saving Juno."

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.200
I didn't know what he meant.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.434
I didn't know if he meant,
"Thanks for saving the movie."

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:45.501
-Yeah.
-Like I was the saving grace.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:46.801
Or "Thanks for saving
the character,"

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.968
which doesn't make any sense.
-No, but doesn't matter.

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:50.901
-I think he was just reaching
for anything to say

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.267
and he maybe didn't remember
the specifics of the movie.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.534
-I'll take it.
-So I said, "What do you mean?"

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.133
And I shouldn't have said that.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.534
I think I've learned since then,
just say, "Thanks, Mel,"

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:01.868
and high-five
and just be friends

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.767
and don't create a weird --
-Don't question it, yeah.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.367
-Yeah, move forward.
You must have learned this.

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:07.267
-Did you move on after that.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.467
-Yeah, we powered through it.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.501
Yeah, he kind of, you know,
shrugged it off.

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.667
And we recovered
and had a good time.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.434
-Yeah, I mean, that's kind of
a great memory of Mel Brooks.

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:18.234
You go in, you have weird
small talk, and then you leave.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.133
-And then he signed
all these box sets for us.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.400
He was like, "Here,
take this, take this."

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.667
-He signed you --
-Yes.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.334
And actually he didn't even
have his new one on him.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.634
He's like, "I would love
to give you my new one."

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.567
He didn't have it,
and then we were walking out,

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.734
and he was, like, running across
the parking lot at us --

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.567
"I found one, I found one,
I found one."

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.334
-Mel Brooks
is running after you?

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:35.033
-No, he was great.
-I love this.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:36.200
-He's an amazing guy,

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.534
and, you know, meeting him
was incredible.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.067
He's, like,
a total hero of mine.

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:42.534
-Do you like doing
animated films?

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:43.734
-It's great, it's great.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:46.133
It's actually, you know, like,
really hard work.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.767
Like, you kind of feel
physically exhausted after it.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:52.400
More so than, you know, being on
set for like a 12-hour day even.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.734
-Really?
-Because they just kind of --

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:56.767
Well, especially this one
when I'm playing a dog, Hank.

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.934
And -- Like, from the title.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.100
"Legend of Hank."

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.067
-Yeah. You are hank.
-I am Hank.

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:04.400
-It's you speaking
into a microphone.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.200
-Yeah.
-And you're exhausted by it.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.767
-Well, okay.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.000
Not the whole thing.
But, like, sometimes they say --

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.667
You know, there's, like,
action sequences in this movie.

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:12.934
They go, "Okay,
now we just need you --

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:15.400
Michael, we need, like, a bank
of exertion noises

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.901
or, like, doggy panting."

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:19.734
So you just stand there at
the mic for a half hour going

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:22.467
[Grunting]

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:23.934
And you're doing that
for a half-hour.

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:25.334
-Okay.
-And by the end of it,

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:27.100
you're like, "Guys, I --
we need to stop."

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.534
Like, "I can't --"
-"I'm gonna pass out."

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:30.601
-You're hyperventilating.

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:31.868
-Yeah, I gave
as much as I can give.

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:33.000
What more do you want?
-Yes.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.100
-What do you want?
-It ain't for wimps.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.901
-$1,433? Come on.

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:40.167
I'm giving you grunts here
and pants like a dog, yeah.

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:42.567
It's super cute.
It's super fun.

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.200
It's action-packed.
-Yeah.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.534
-The idea is that Hank
wants to be a samurai.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.334
-Yes.
-It's not easy.

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:51.667
-No.
-No, so this is --

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.868
Yeah, this is "Paws of Fury:
The Legend of Hank."

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:55.601
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Michael Cera.

00:06:55.601 --> 00:06:58.067
Check it out.

00:06:58.067 --> 00:06:59.133
-What's that?

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.701
-The blindfold
is to help you focus.

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:03.534
-Ah.
-Now listen.

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:06.901
Tell me what you hear.
-I hear you talking and moving.

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:07.767
-Good.
[ Bird squawks ]

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:09.300
-I hear a bird.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.501
-That's it.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.868
-I smell flowers, actually.

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:14.667
-Dogs have a keen sense of smell
and excellent hearing.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.701
-I hear a dragonfly.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.300
[ Buzzing ]

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.501
[ Sniffing ]

00:07:18.501 --> 00:07:20.000
I smell wood burning.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.033
[ Kettle whistling ]
Smell tea brewing.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.334
[ Sniffing ]

00:07:24.334 --> 00:07:25.767
Hey, are you making nachos?

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:29.601
'Cause someone
just cut the cheese.

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:31.601
-Lesson over.

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:32.634
Well done.

00:07:32.634 --> 00:07:34.000
-Yeah, it is well done.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.334
That's how you do it
right there.

00:07:36.334 --> 00:07:38.601
Michael Cera, everybody.

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:39.901
I love having you on.

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:43.367
"Paws of Fury: The Legend
of Hank" is in theaters now.

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:45.133
We'll be right back
with Keke Palmer, everyone.

00:07:45.133 --> 00:07:45.968
Stick around.

